      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wondering why the integration test module doesn\u0027t require a customized \"test_config\" (e.g. AndroidTest.xml) similar to https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Connectivity/thread/tests/unit/AndroidTest.xml. For example, the integration test needs to access to the hidden API, which requires `\u003coption name\u003d\"hidden-api-checks\" value\u003d\"false\"/\u003e` in AndroidTest.xml. Second example is that guava tests will bed added to `ThreadNetworkIntegrationTests` when it links the guava library, so we need\n\n```\n\u003c!-- Ignores tests introduced by guava-android-testlib --\u003e\n\u003coption name\u003d\"exclude-annotation\" value\u003d\"org.junit.Ignore\"/\u003e\n```\nin the AndroidTest.xml. Can you double check that you don\u0027t have those issues without AndroidTest.xml?",
